// Probe 16 — Cluster I LHS border: call returning a literal `"const" ?? "x"`
//
// The callee returns a static string literal.  At runtime, the returned
// Str's ptr points into `.rodata` (program-lifetime), not into a heap
// String.  If the cluster I bug only fires for HEAP-backed sources, this
// probe ESCAPES — the OpFreeText on `_ncc_N` runs but the actual bytes
// live forever in the binary's `.rodata`.
//
// If 16 FAILS like 05, the bug is shape-only (not allocation-class):
// even a static-source `_ncc_N` triggers the dangling-Str escape because
// the bytecode dispatcher doesn't distinguish heap-vs-static Str at the
// scope-exit-free site.
// If 16 PASSES while 05 fails, the bug is allocation-class-dependent —
// fix can be narrower.
//
// Pairing: diff against 05 (call returning a non-static heap String).
// Status: cluster I LHS-border probe; separates shape from allocation.

fn static_text() -> text {
  return "present";
}

fn main() {
  a = static_text() ?? "fallback";
  assert(a == "present", "probe 16: got '{a}', want 'present'");
  println("probe 16 PASSED");
}
